  "notes": "COMPOUND VERB:\n{駆|か}ける (to run, to gallop) + {込|こ}む (into)\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n{自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive) - takes に for the destination\n\nRELATED NOUN:\n- {駆|か}け{込|こ}み: last-minute rush\n- {駆|か}け{込|こ}み{乗車|じょうしゃ}: rushing onto a train (discouraged by station announcements)\n- {駆|か}け{込|こ}み{寺|でら}: refuge temple (historically for women seeking divorce)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {駆|か}け{込|こ}みセーフ: just barely making it\n- {駆|か}け{込|こ}み{需要|じゅよう}: last-minute demand (before a deadline or price increase)",
